<title>AUSTRALIA: AUSTRIM NOT TO MOP UP HAWKER STRAGGLERS.</title>
<headline>AUSTRIM NOT TO MOP UP HAWKER STRAGGLERS.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Manufacturer and investment group Austrim Ltd said on Friday it held an 87.78 percent stake in auto parts manufacturer Hawker Richardson Ltd and would not be proceeding to compulsory acquisition.</p>
<p>Australian corporations law requires that a bidder must have 90 percent or more of the issued capital before compulsory acquisition can proceeed.</p>
<p>Austrim's A$1.86 per share takeover offer closed on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
